#!/bin/sh
# Refuse a push that nobody asked for.
#
# release-please reads the subjects on `main`, so a push moves the release PR; and a
# checkout that is many commits behind its remote publishes all of them at once. An agent
# landing a branch into local `main` is finished there.
#
# A person pushing on purpose sets ML_STACK_PUSH=yes for that one command:
#
#     ML_STACK_PUSH=yes git push
[ "$ML_STACK_PUSH" = yes ] && exit 0
cat >&2 <<'WHY'
pre-push: refused.

A push is the repository owner's to make. release-please reads the commit subjects on
`main`, so pushing moves the release pull request, and a local `main` that is ahead
publishes every commit on it at once.

Land your branch into local `main` and stop there. Say in your report that it is unpushed.

To push on purpose:  ML_STACK_PUSH=yes git push
WHY
exit 1
